# 6. Design Philosophy

The framework follows six principles.

## 6.1 Observe Before Acting

A security mechanism should collect sufficient evidence before taking consequential action.

## 6.2 Validate Before Escalating

Detection does not automatically imply threat.

The framework therefore separates:

> Detection ≠ Validation ≠ Classification

This reduces the possibility of treating every anomaly as a confirmed security incident.

## 6.3 Learn From Previous Encounters

Previous security events should contribute to future analysis and policy improvement.

## 6.4 Test Before Adaptation

A proposed security-policy modification should be evaluated before becoming an active policy.

## 6.5 Adapt With Governance

Adaptation should not mean unrestricted autonomous modification.

Every important change should remain:

* traceable,
* testable,
* reversible,
* auditable.

## 6.6 Continuous Feedback

The outcome of security actions should feed back into future monitoring and analysis.

