# 25. Human-in-the-Loop Governance

The framework supports different levels of autonomy.

### Level 0 — Manual

All security decisions require human action.

### Level 1 — Assisted

The framework detects and recommends actions.

### Level 2 — Controlled Automation

Low-risk actions may be automatically executed.

### Level 3 — Adaptive Automation

Validated policies may automatically adapt within predefined boundaries.

### Level 4 — Governed Autonomous Security

The framework continuously detects, validates, tests, adapts, and monitors within formally defined constraints, while retaining human oversight for exceptional or high-impact decisions.

The intended architecture is therefore:

> **Autonomy within boundaries, not autonomy without governance.**

---

# 26. Security Policy Governance

Every adaptive policy should satisfy five governance requirements.

## 26.1 Traceability

The reason for every policy modification must be identifiable.

## 26.2 Validation

Evidence supporting the modification must be available.

## 26.3 Testing

The proposed policy must pass defined tests.

## 26.4 Reversibility

The previous policy version must remain recoverable.

## 26.5 Accountability

The system must identify whether an action was:

* human initiated,
* AI recommended,
* automatically executed,
* automatically rolled back.

