# 32. Security Effectiveness Metrics

The framework can be evaluated using quantitative metrics.

### Detection Rate

$$
DR = \frac{TP}{TP+FN}
$$

### Precision

$$
Precision = \frac{TP}{TP+FP}
$$

### False Positive Rate

$$
FPR = \frac{FP}{FP+TN}
$$

### Mean Time to Detect

$$
MTTD = T_{detection}-T_{event}
$$

### Mean Time to Respond

$$
MTTR = T_{response}-T_{detection}
$$

### Adaptation Success Rate

$$
ASR = \frac{Successful\ Adaptations}{Total\ Adaptation\ Attempts}
$$

### Rollback Rate

$$
RR = \frac{Rollback\ Events}{Total\ Deployments}
$$

### Policy Stability

Policy stability measures how frequently policies change over a defined period.

Excessive adaptation may indicate instability, while insufficient adaptation may indicate an inability to respond to environmental changes.

